# Git Commit Author, Committer, and Push Identity

This repo is owned by **tmwclaxton**. Commits and pushes must use that account only. Never attribute or authenticate as `toby`, `tobyclaxton`, or `toby.claxton@*`.

`--author` alone is not enough: Git still records the Committer from local `user.name` / `user.email`, which often shows up as Toby on GitHub.

## Identity to use

```text
tmwclaxton <57643714+tmwclaxton@users.noreply.github.com>
```

## Before every push (required)

Run these checks and **do not push** until they pass:

1. Active GitHub CLI user is tmwclaxton:

```bash
gh api user --jq .login
# must print: tmwclaxton
```

2. `origin` points at the tmwclaxton repo (not a fork under another login):

```bash
git remote get-url origin
# must contain: github.com/tmwclaxton/snitch
```

3. Commits about to be pushed are not attributed to toby / cineark:

```bash
git log origin/main..HEAD --format='Author: %an <%ae>%nCommitter: %cn <%ce>'
# Author and Committer must be tmwclaxton / 57643714+tmwclaxton@users.noreply.github.com
# (GitHub <noreply@github.com> as Committer on merge commits is fine)
```

If `gh` is logged in as `tobyclaxton`, switch or log out first:

```bash
gh auth switch --user tmwclaxton
# or: gh auth logout --user tobyclaxton
```

## How to detect availability for commits

Prefer this identity when any of the following is true:

1. `gh api user --jq .login` returns `tmwclaxton`
2. The remote is under `github.com/tmwclaxton/`
3. The user asks to commit/push as tmwclaxton

If none of those apply, fall back to the repository's existing git author / user rules and do not invent an identity.

## How to apply on commit

Set Author **and** Committer via env vars on every commit (do not rely on `--author` alone):

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="tmwclaxton" \
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="57643714+tmwclaxton@users.noreply.github.com" \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="tmwclaxton" \
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="57643714+tmwclaxton@users.noreply.github.com" \
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Commit message here.

EOF
)"
```

- Do **not** run `git config` to change global or local `user.name` / `user.email` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do **not** commit with Author or Committer as `toby`, `tobyclaxton`, or any `toby.claxton@*` email.
- After committing, verify with `git log -1 --format='Author: %an <%ae>%nCommitter: %cn <%ce>'`.
- If a commit was just created in this conversation with wrong Author/Committer and has not been pushed, amend with the same env vars and `--reset-author` (only when amend rules allow).
- If it was already pushed and the user wants attribution fixed, ask before force-pushing; on `main`/`master` only force-push when the user explicitly approves.

## Pushing

Push to `origin` on `github.com/tmwclaxton/snitch` only. Do not change remotes unless the user asks. Do not push while authenticated as `tobyclaxton`.
